   272	both a rejected case and a passing residual at the current constants).
   273	Authorship fraud, paraphrase and freshly composed filler are out of scope.
   274	The baseline rule trusts the reviewed trunk and
   275	its `origin/master` ref; hostile ref/history fabrication is not prevented.
   276	No attestation or tamper-resistant provenance is claimed. The censor and
   277	Patron retain responsibility for the substance and attribution of evidence.
   278	
   279	`opus.ui.rulings` checks present references in every state, and requires a
   280	nonempty list with a current ruling at done. `done` refuses an absent list,
   281	wrong actor/opus, empty or dead decision, or a list containing only wrong-tree
   282	or too-early rulings before any write or event. A generic
   283	human waiver does not satisfy this requirement: any Patron exception is
   284	itself a recorded, scoped look-and-feel ruling. A new source tree requires
   285	new served evidence and new Patron rulings; old decisions remain history.
   286	
   287	### 3. An arc is a parent reference, not a new lifecycle
   288	
   289	An arc is an ordinary `opera/W-*.md` record with `kind: arc`, its own title,
   290	optional body, collegium, state and the existing lifecycle obligations.
   291	No new id allocator, directory or lifecycle is needed. Membership is the
   292	optional scalar `arc: W-123` on a non-arc opus; it must resolve to an arc
   293	record in the same officina. Arcs themselves cannot name an arc or parent.
   294	There are no roll-ups, inferred completion or nested arcs in this opus.
   295	
   296	`parent: W-124` is required for `subtask`, forbidden for other kinds, and
   297	must resolve to a non-arc, non-subtask opus in the same officina. This makes
   298	subtasks one level deep, with no cycles or self-parenting. A subtask may omit
   299	`arc` and inherit its parent's membership in the model; if it explicitly
   300	sets `arc`, that reference must equal the parent's arc. If the parent has no
   301	arc, the subtask cannot introduce one. No inherited value is written back.
   302	
   303	`opus.arc` and `opus.parent` block malformed, dangling, wrong-kind, cross-
   304	officina and conflicting references. Resolve validated ids against an
   305	enumerated record map, never arbitrary paths. Hierarchy does not imply
   306	`depends`, change WIP accounting or constrain parent/child completion order;
   307	dependency scheduling remains W-068.
   308	
   309	Physical containment applies to all W-096 reference readers: opus records,
   310	parent/arc targets, spec briefs, UI input/censor/served logs and decisions.
   311	Use existing safe-path helpers plus lstat and realpath checks before reading:
   312	regular files only, no symlink leaf or intervening symlink directories, and
   313	real paths contained under the selected officina and expected subdirectory
   314	(`opera`, `briefs`, `ci`, `decisions`). Reject escaping, dangling or aliased
   315	paths even when their ids are lexically valid. Enforce in check enumeration
   316	and all affected writers/transition readers, not just after loading a record
   317	map. Report `opus.reference` (block) for unsafe files, with the field-specific
   318	rule as appropriate; unreadable required evidence fails closed. This bounds
   319	W-096 reads; adapter snapshot/server delivery hardening remains the named
   320	“Reject symlinked opus records before snapshot projection and detail delivery”
   321	follow-on. This does not claim protection against concurrent hostile writers.
   322	
   323	### 4. Start/end are optional actual dates, never guessed history
   324	
   325	Canonical fields are `start` and `end`, each an optional scalar string in
   326	this exact ISO-8601 UTC profile:
   327	`^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])T([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]:[0-5][0-9](\.[0-9]{3})?Z$`.
   328	Years are 0001–9999; validate actual Gregorian month lengths and leap years
   329	(divisible by 4, except centuries unless divisible by 400). Reject year 0000,
   330	24:00, leap seconds, offsets including +00:00/-00:00, lowercase t/z, missing
   331	seconds, fractional precision other than exactly three, and date-only values.
   332	Absent milliseconds mean zero. Writers emit exactly three fractional digits.
   333	Inspect the YAML scalar node's decoded string and match this regex before
   334	calendar validation; reject explicit non-string tags, aliases and coercion
   335	to Date objects. Quoted and plain string scalars are equally legal; quote
   336	style is not enforced. Do not validate by permissive `Date` parsing or
   337	normalization. Compare validated components/numeric instants for ordering.
   338	The same profile governs new UI evidence and ruling timestamps. Validate
   339	lifecycle `--now` under this profile before conversion or any mutation.
   340	When both exist, end must be at or after start; end without start is valid
   341	for an older active opus whose beginning was never recorded. `end` is valid
   342	only in `done`; absence of either field is legal, including on old done
   343	records. Rules: `opus.dates` and `opus.dates.order`.
   344	
   345	Derive new dates from successful lifecycle transitions: `ready` records the
   346	first start when absent, and `done` records end, using exactly the timestamp
   347	emitted with that transition. Resuming a halt preserves start; a failed
   348	review reopening done clears end and preserves start; a later done stamps
   349	a new end. These are persisted transition facts so losing the local event
   350	log does not lose dates. Refused commands change neither dates nor events.
   351	Validate supplied existing dates before a transition could overwrite them.
   352	
   353	Do not backfill from mtime, traditio, first observation, `item_appeared`, or
   354	snapshot-derived event times (`workflow.time.derived`). Start/end are actuals,
   355	not planned dates or deadlines; planned dates would be a separate decree.
   356	
   357	### 5. Summary is title; description is the Markdown body
   358	
   359	There is exactly one summary source: existing front-matter `title`, a
   360	nonblank string containing no forbidden controls after YAML decoding. The
   361	exact forbidden set is U+0000–U+001F (C0, including NUL, TAB, LF and CR),
   362	U+007F–U+009F (DEL and C1), U+2028–U+2029, and these format-control ranges:
   363	U+00AD, U+0600–U+0605, U+061C, U+06DD, U+070F, U+0890–U+0891, U+08E2,
   364	U+180E, U+200B–U+200F, U+202A–U+202E, U+2060–U+2064, U+2066–U+206F,
   365	U+FEFF, U+FFF9–U+FFFB, U+110BD, U+110CD, U+13430–U+1343F,
   366	U+1BCA0–U+1BCA3, U+1D173–U+1D17A, U+E0001 and U+E0020–U+E007F.
   367	This explicit set includes bidi controls and is frozen, not dependent on the
   368	runtime Unicode property's version. Validate code points, including astral
   369	ones, at both disk and writer boundaries. “One line” is a
   370	logical field constraint, not a character limit or a prohibition on visual
   371	wrapping. Long existing titles, including W-096's decree, remain intact.
   372	`opus.title` blocks control-bearing/blank/nonstring titles; `newItem`, `runNew`
   373	and `amend --title` reject them before writing.
   374	
   375	Description is all authored Markdown below the front-matter delimiter. Empty
   376	is legal; it is not derived from title or `spec`, and no `summary:` or
   377	`description:` duplicate field is introduced. Existing body-preserving
   378	mutation stays byte-for-byte. Do not alter W-087's bounded HTTP body reader,
   379	its truncation marker, literal rendering, whitespace or summary/title layout.
