     8	 * back into an opus and committing it changes the hash every later
     9	 * `verify`/`check` compares against — a certificate goes stale just because
    10	 * `verify` ran — and (b) a dirty tree caused only by that same bookkeeping
    11	 * would wrongly refuse to certify at all.
    12	 *
    13	 * `sourceTreeHash` instead hashes `git ls-tree -r <ref>` with the studio
    14	 * dir and `.bisellium/` excluded, so committing studio bookkeeping never
    15	 * moves it; `isDirtyOutside` is the matching working-tree check, ignoring
    16	 * uncommitted changes under those same paths.
    17	 */
